# Paths that must never leave this repository inside a `git archive` export.
#
# The ITP artifact is a release snapshot of the mathematical development, cut
# by scripts/make_artifact.sh; docs/ARTIFACT.md says what it contains and why.
# That script already restricts the export to an explicit allow-list, so these
# attributes are the second, independent guard: they also keep a plain
# `git archive` (or a GitHub "Download source" tarball of a release) free of
# the AI-workflow layer.
#
# Keep the two in step: a path excluded here and a path missing from the
# script's INCLUDE list should describe the same snapshot.  This list is a
# deny-list, so it is the weaker of the two guards: a new workflow-only path
# joins a plain `git archive` until it is named here, while the script's
# allow-list drops it on its own.

# --- AI-workflow layer: the machinery that produced the development ---------
local/                  export-ignore
results/                export-ignore
.github/                export-ignore
.githooks/              export-ignore
.claude/                export-ignore
.codex/                 export-ignore
audits/                 export-ignore
docbuild/               export-ignore
home_page/              export-ignore
AGENTS.md               export-ignore
CLAUDE.md               export-ignore
texra-blueprint.toml    export-ignore

# --- workflow-only scripts --------------------------------------------------
# `scripts/` is mixed: `scripts/comparator/`, the blueprint axiom audit and its
# Python helpers, and this packaging script ship with the artifact; the rest serve the
# workflow layer.  `git archive` does not descend into an ignored directory, so
# a child of `scripts/ export-ignore` could not be re-admitted; the workflow-only
# scripts are excluded by glob instead and the four shipped top-level files are
# re-admitted with `-export-ignore`.  `scripts/comparator/` is never matched.
scripts/*.py            export-ignore
scripts/*.sh            export-ignore
scripts/*.lean          export-ignore
scripts/tests/          export-ignore
scripts/blueprint_leanok_axioms.py -export-ignore
scripts/blueprint_lean_sync.py -export-ignore
scripts/tex_utils.py     -export-ignore
scripts/make_artifact.sh -export-ignore

# --- repository plumbing ----------------------------------------------------
.gitignore              export-ignore
.gitattributes          export-ignore

# --- workflow-only docs -----------------------------------------------------
docs/campaign/                  export-ignore
docs/reports/                   export-ignore
docs/ci-automation.md           export-ignore
docs/ci-blueprint-sync.md       export-ignore
docs/pr_review_management.md    export-ignore
docs/stale_issue_audit.md       export-ignore
docs/blueprint-script-coverage.md export-ignore

# --- third-party paper sources: NOT ignored, on purpose ---------------------
# `references/` ships with the artifact (owner decision, 2026-09-19, following
# the companion LDT repository).  The Lean docstrings, the theorem index and the
# deviations page cite `references/<paper>/<file>.tex:<lines>`, so a snapshot
# without them cannot be checked against its sources.  They are third-party
# material kept for reference, not covered by this repository's licence; see
# docs/ARTIFACT.md.  Listed here so that nobody adds `export-ignore` back
# without reading that decision.

# --- generated or workflow-only build products ------------------------------
blueprint/web/          export-ignore
blueprint/lean_decls    export-ignore
proof-guide-bridge-lemmas-sorry-elim.md export-ignore
